  "HDDS-13890": {
    "jira_id": "HDDS-13890",
    "issue_type": "New Feature",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Datanode supports dynamic configuration of SCM",
    "description": "Currently if we would like to migrate the SCM from (scm1, scm2, scm3) to (scm4, scm5, scm6), all the datanodes need to be restarted 2 times with updated \"ozone.scm.nodes.<service>\" configuration\r\n\r\n # Before migration: Update ozone.scm.nodes to (scm1, scm2, scm3, scm4, scm5, scm6)\r\n # After (scm1, scm2, scm3) are decommissioned: Update ozone.scm.nodes to (scm4, scm5, scm6)\r\n\r\nAs mentioned in HDDS-12391, rolling restarting all the datanodes might take a while. For large datanodes fleet this might take a lot of time (days or even weeks).\r\n\r\nIt might be good to support dynamic reconfiguration of SCM endpoints in DN to prevent restarts. A possible flow\r\n # Admin update the \"ozone.scm.nodes\" to the new value (with some new nodes and removed nodes)\r\n # DN will compare the new and previous configuration and find the SCM endpoints to add and remove\r\n # DN will add the SCM endpoints (e.g. SCMConnectionManager#addSCMServer) and then remove the SCM endpoints (e.g. SCMConnectionManager#removeSCMServer).",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "94875d9bc5948d876850467fb96d807c9b1512e9",
        "message": "Remove the endpoint first before closing",
        "author": "ivandika3",
        "date": "2025-12-14T05:14:06Z",
        "files": [
